## Executive Summary

Gemini 3 Pro is Google's flagship reasoning model from their Gemini 3 series, designed for complex problem-solving and advanced reasoning tasks. It features a massive 1M token context window, competitive pricing ($2/$12 per 1M tokens up to 200K context), and exceptional performance on reasoning benchmarks (77.1% on ARC-AGI-2, 94.3% on GPQA Diamond). The model was upgraded to Gemini 3.1 Pro in February 2026, which offers significantly better performance across reasoning benchmarks. Gemini 3 Pro (and 3.1 Pro) leads every current frontier model on ARC-AGI-2 by a meaningful margin (77.1% vs Claude Opus 4.6's 68.8% and GPT-5.2's 52.9%). The model ranks #4 of 10 on BenchLM with a score of 77.1/100 and achieves 22.3 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index (78th percentile). Gemini 3 Pro is positioned as Google's most intelligent and adaptive model, capable of helping with real-world complexity and solving problems that require enhanced reasoning and multimodal capabilities.

---

## Model Identity and Background

**Developer:** Google DeepMind
**Release Date:** November 18, 2025 (upgraded to 3.1 Pro in February 2026)
**Series:** Gemini Pro (Gemini 3 Pro / 3.1 Pro)
**Predecessor:** Gemini 2.5 Pro
**Successor:** Gemini 3.1 Pro (February 2026)
**License:** Proprietary
**Context Window:** 1,000,000 tokens
**Max Output:** 32,768 tokens

Gemini 3 Pro is Google's flagship reasoning model from their Gemini 3 series, released in November 2025. It was upgraded to Gemini 3.1 Pro in February 2026, which offers significantly better performance across reasoning benchmarks. The ".1" version increment signals a focused intelligence upgrade rather than a broad feature expansion. Gemini 3 Pro (and 3.1 Pro) represents a significant advancement in Google's reasoning capabilities, with the ".1" version more than doubling reasoning performance on ARC-AGI-2 from 31.1% (Gemini 3 Pro) to 77.1% (Gemini 3.1 Pro). The model is designed for tasks where a simple answer isn't enough and requires advanced reasoning, such as synthesizing data or explaining complex topics.

